results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:6:| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | **22** (21.0%) | 102 | 3: SendInterviewEmailTask (ask_user_without_simulator), CheckInvoiceTask2 (unsupported_action), ThanksgivingPrepTask (setup_failed) | 16 (8) | 15 (14) | 148 |
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:7:| MAI-UI-2B | **11** (10.5%) | 98 | 7: MattermostReadingGroupTask (ask_user_without_simulator), ReadQwen3PaperTask4 (setup_failed), ReadQwen3PaperTask5 (setup_failed), ReadQwen3PaperTask3 (setup_failed), ReadQwen3PaperTask1 (setup_failed), SendFormsTask (setup_failed), ThanksgivingPrepTask (setup_failed) | 40 (8) | 19 (14) | 175 |
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:9:Paired on the same 105 tasks: both solved 6, v4 only 0, GUI-Owl only 16, neither 83; difference -15.2 pp, exact McNemar p = 3.05e-05 (conditional on these task pairs; one run per model).
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:11:Sensitivity (environment): excluding the 8 tasks with a folder-level setup/scoring failure in either run, v4 6 vs GUI-Owl 22 of 97; also excluding tasks with a device-health re-initialisation (18 tasks), v4 5 vs GUI-Owl 21 of 87. Excluding known errors cannot show that the remaining tasks were unaffected; GUI-Owl's container had more environment failures than v4's.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:13:MAI-UI-2B vs v4 (paired, 105 tasks): both 4, MAI-UI only 7, v4 only 2; difference +4.8 pp, exact McNemar p = 0.18.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:14:MAI-UI-2B vs GUI-Owl (paired, 105 tasks): both 9, MAI-UI only 2, GUI-Owl only 13; difference -10.5 pp, exact McNemar p = 0.00739.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:16:MAI-UI's run ended 6 tasks without a result after setup failures (ReadQwen3PaperTask1, ReadQwen3PaperTask3, ReadQwen3PaperTask4, ReadQwen3PaperTask5, SendFormsTask, ThanksgivingPrepTask; GUI-Owl and v4: ThanksgivingPrepTask only). Excluding them: MAI-UI 11 vs v4 6 vs GUI-Owl 22 of 99. MAI-UI ran after the other two, on recreated containers after two spot preemptions, so its environment was not identical.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:18:Infrastructure: ReadQwen3PaperTask1, ReadQwen3PaperTask3, ReadQwen3PaperTask4, ReadQwen3PaperTask5, SendFormsTask never had a working device. The emulator in container lfmenv_0 (MAI-UI's half b) had died with a fatal KVM error (`kvm_user_backed_ram_map: error registering slot: File exists`), so every /task/init returned 500, including the one fresh-container attempt the completion rule allows. Under the rule they count as failures. Upper bound if all of them had succeeded: MAI-UI 16 vs GUI-Owl 22 (-5.7 pp, McNemar p = 0.263); GUI-Owl and v4 solved none of these tasks. MAI-UI trails GUI-Owl even in that best case, but whether the gap is significant depends on these tasks.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:23:* GUI-Owl-1.5-2B: earlier folders ended setup_failed 12, ask_user_without_simulator 6, unsupported_action 5, scoring_failed 3, invalid_model_output 2; successes after an earlier failed folder: none; successes after a device-health re-initialisation: SendWaiverTask.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:24:* MAI-UI-2B: earlier folders ended setup_failed 34, ask_user_without_simulator 13, interrupted 4; successes after an earlier failed folder: none; successes after a device-health re-initialisation: none.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:25:* GUI-Owl's official agent returns an `error_env` sentinel after 5 unparseable outputs, which MobileWorld's own action validator rejects (an upstream bug), so instead of ending and being scored the task was re-executed (2 executions); those tasks still scored 0.
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:26:* `ask_user` needs an LLM-backed user simulator this setup does not have: 7 GUI-Owl executions and 14 MAI-UI executions hit it (v4 has no such action). `double_tap` was rejected by GUI-Owl's official action adapter (not by the runtime).
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:30:| Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl (official agent) | MAI-UI (official agent) |
results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:39:MobileWorld's own `--auto_retry 3` (same flag in every run) re-runs a task whose execution ended without a result, whatever the reason; mw_resume.sh then applied the pre-declared completion rule (docs/PREREG_v4.md 2026-11-19 01:55, clarified 05:45: the fresh-container allowance is one more invocation, inside which `--auto_retry 3` allows up to 4 executions, equally for every model). Single run per model at temperature 0; a secondary, descriptive benchmark comparing agent pipelines, not model weights alone. Independent recomputation: results/codex/mw_r2_audit/ (VALID WITH CAVEATS).
