--- /dev/null
+++ b/results/codex/mw_maiui_audit/report.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS.** MAI-UI's **11/105**, all three paired comparisons, and the recorded completion decisions are reproducible. The addition is valid as a descriptive comparison of the configured pipelines. Its account of five tasks that “never had a working device” is contradicted by the trajectories. No P1 finding; one P2 reporting defect and one P3 snapshot defect below. Neither warrants changing the recorded scores.
+
+Offline audit of the supplied local snapshot and clean MobileWorld checkout `a026188705f4a494a12d14ddab3786a23fd2c537`. No VM, Colab, emulator, server, or process was contacted/signalled. Writes are confined to this directory. Task-log timestamps below are **UTC on 2026-11-19**; add eight hours for the watcher/PREREG's Manila times.
+
+1. **P2 — The crash disclosure assigns the wrong container, erases usable attempts, and dates the final failure too early.** The assertion appears in [PREREG_v4.md:349](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:349), [comparison.md:18](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md:18), [STATUS.md:29](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/STATUS.md:29), and [snapshot.json:38](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/snapshot.json:38). The generator labels **every final setup failure except Thanksgiving** an emulator-crash task, without consulting its container or earlier executions ([mw_summarize_r2.py:196](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/mw_summarize_r2.py:196), [emitted assertion:250](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/mw_summarize_r2.py:250)).
+
+   | Disclosed task | Actual half | Attempts with model actions / total recorded actions | First such attempt starts |
+   |---|---|---:|---|
+   | [ReadQwen3PaperTask1](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask1_backup_20261119_111404/thread_128020089180288.log:42) | b | 1 / 4 | 09:06:59 |
+   | [ReadQwen3PaperTask3](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask3_backup_20261119_111225/traj.json:7) | b | 2 / 7 | 08:46:36 |
+   | [ReadQwen3PaperTask4](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask4_backup_20261119_113014/thread_131368874643584.log:107) | b | 3 / 9 | 08:02:21 |
+   | [ReadQwen3PaperTask5](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask5_backup_20261119_103237/thread_133568918093952.log:1) | **a: mobile_world_env_0** | **5 / 20** | 07:42:13 |
+   | [SendFormsTask](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/SendFormsTask_backup_20261119_111509/thread_128020089180288.log:8) | b | 0 / 0 | None; first setup fails at 09:07–09:08 |
+
+   All eleven action-bearing attempts of those four Qwen tasks ended at `ask_user` because the user simulator lacked an API key. For example, Task5 successfully executed clicks, then received that distinct HTTP-500/401 failure ([log:57](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask5_backup_20261119_103237/thread_133568918093952.log:57), [log:228](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask5_backup_20261119_103237/thread_133568918093952.log:228)). Task5's failures cannot be attributed to the later KVM event in the other container.
+
+   Half b's additional invocation also **started with a working device**: ReadQwen3PaperTask2 initialized at **11:18:32**, ran 50 steps, and scored zero at **11:27:19** ([initialization:6](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask2/thread_131368874643584.log:6), [score:3726](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask2/thread_131368874643584.log:3726)). Task4 then recovered an initial health failure and executed three actions through **11:28:50** ([recovery:16](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask4_backup_20261119_113014/thread_131368874643584.log:16)). The subsequent Task3 execution initialized at **11:28:58**, lost screenshot/device health by **11:29:14**, and then failed `/task/init` at **11:29:55** ([log:6](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask3_backup_20261119_113023/thread_131368874643584.log:6)). All remaining executions of Task1/3/4 and SendForms failed setup through 11:32:02. Thus the evidence supports a failure **during** that invocation, not a dead emulator when it launched at 19:18 Manila.
+
+   **Correction:** describe mixed model/user-simulator and environment failures, distinguish halves and episodes, and replace “never had a working device” with the actual final dispositions. The Docker/emulator logs containing the quoted KVM error are absent from the supplied artifacts; the pull script copies trajectories/manifests/markers, not those logs ([mw_pull_r2.sh:13](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/mw_pull_r2.sh:13)). The client evidence corroborates loss of device health, but cannot independently establish that fatal error's cause or exact onset. Retain the five-task bound as an explicitly conditional sensitivity, not a general bound on a healthy run.
+
+2. **P3 — Repeated pulls leave a stale log in a final folder, confusing attempt chronology.** The pull merges into an existing destination without deleting files moved away remotely ([mw_pull_r2.sh:13](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/mw_pull_r2.sh:13)). GUI-Owl's final Thanksgiving folder contains both the [old 20:38:54 log](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/guiowl_gui_en_r2/ThanksgivingPrepTask/thread_140161534165120.log:1) and the [new 02:13:21 log](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/guiowl_gui_en_r2/ThanksgivingPrepTask/thread_129745380753536.log:1). The old file is byte-identical to its [moved archive](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_interrupted/guiowl/ThanksgivingPrepTask_20261119_021248/thread_140161534165120.log:1). Sorting filenames and taking the last error consequently selects the **old** execution ([mw_summarize_r2.py:42](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/mw_summarize_r2.py:42)). Both ended `setup_failed`, so this changes no score/category here; no equivalent duplicate was found for MAI-UI. Use a new snapshot destination or reconcile stale files before treating final-folder contents as an execution history. The independent audit deduplicates this exact archived copy.
+
+**Independent score and inventory checks.** The master manifest has 105 unique tasks. The saved halves are exactly its alternating **53 + 52**, disjoint, and each task has one canonical MAI-UI folder in its expected container. Half a contributes 50 result files/8 successes; half b 48/3. All **304 result.txt files** across the three arms contain a valid binary score agreeing with the task log; none occurs in a backup or moved folder. No observed result should be discarded or substituted. In particular, Task2's zero remains a valid recorded result. The seven MAI-UI tasks without results are the six final setup failures already listed in the comparison plus MattermostReadingGroupTask (`ask_user_without_simulator`).
+
+| Arm | Successes / 105 | Result files | No result | Attempt folders | Internal health retries |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| MAI-UI | 11 (10.4762%) | 98 | 7 | 156 | 19 |
+| v4 | 6 (5.7143%) | 104 | 1 | 112 | 2 |
+| GUI-Owl | 22 (20.9524%) | 102 | 3 | 133 | 15 |
+
+| A minus B | Both | A only | B only | Neither | Difference, pp | Exact two-sided McNemar p |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| v4 − GUI-Owl | 6 | 0 | 16 | 83 | −15.238095 | 0.000030517578125 |
+| MAI-UI − v4 | 4 | 7 | 2 | 92 | +4.761905 | 0.1796875 |
+| MAI-UI − GUI-Owl | 9 | 2 | 13 | 81 | −10.476190 | 0.00738525390625 |
+
+These match the summaries, comparison JSON/MD, STATUS and snapshot numbers. Compared with `521d8db~1`, both older per-arm summaries are unchanged except the added zero `model_server_unreachable_folders` field. Excluding MAI-UI's six final setup failures gives **11 vs 6 vs 22 of 99**, as published. Flipping only the specified five zeros gives **16 vs GUI-Owl 22**, −5.714286 pp, **p = 0.26317596435546875**; GUI-Owl and v4 solved none of those five. That arithmetic is fair for that fixed scenario. It does not establish performance after repairing every environment problem or justify an unrestricted “in every case” claim.
+
+**Completion-rule verification.** Every one of the **249 manifest rows** (118 a, 131 b) agrees with the folder state and prior moved attempts at that decision time; see [manifest_checks.json](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/codex/mw_maiui_audit/manifest_checks.json). Eleven folders were moved: four interruptions and seven setup failures. SharePhotosTask/MastodonImportMutedUsersTask were interrupted around the first preemption; CheckInvoiceTask3/MastodonPostEditedPhotoTask around the second. Each was resumed **once**, ended with a zero result, and had no terminal error/result in its interrupted copy ([a decisions:55](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_a.jsonl:55), [a:88](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_a.jsonl:88), [b:53](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_b.jsonl:53), [b:91](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_b.jsonl:91)).
+
+The seven additional setup-failure invocations covered Qwen1–5, SendForms and Thanksgiving, exactly once each ([a:114](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_a.jsonl:114), [b:123](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/_retry_manifest_maiui_b.jsonl:123)). Task2 obtained a result on its first additional execution; the other six used four. Thanksgiving received four original plus four additional executions in **each** arm. This matches the 05:45 clarification: one invocation, with MW's `1 + auto_retry` executions ([runner.py:303](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/tools/MobileWorld/src/mobile_world/core/runner.py:303)), plus internal pre-action health retries. Earlier `ask_user` failures followed by a terminal setup failure were eligible because the declared classifier uses the **last** error, not any historical model failure. No extra allowance, duplicated resume, successful-result rerun, or outcome selection was found. Completion markers are 18:36:14 Manila for a and 19:32:03 for b; both older arms completed before MAI-UI began.
+
+**Other device/server exposure.** Health trouble was intermittent well before the final collapse: first explicit unhealthy responses were **04:02:20 in half a** ([MastodonInviteTask:8](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/MastodonInviteTask/thread_124426108313728.log:8)) and **07:14:20 in half b** ([MattermostCreateChannelTask:8](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/MattermostCreateChannelTask_backup_20261119_110204/thread_128020089180288.log:8)). Half a also suffered separate late setup failures around 10:29 and 10:35. Half b had a failed-setup streak from **11:14:28** before the successful 11:18 restart ([Task1:8](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/mobileworld/traj_r2/maiui_gui_en_r2/ReadQwen3PaperTask1_backup_20261119_111545/thread_128020089180288.log:8)). These are not evidence of one continuously dead device throughout the run.
+
+Nine result-bearing MAI-UI tasks recovered internal health failures: **MastodonInviteTask, MastodonConditionalFavoTask, SuggestPaperTask, CheckInterviewTimesTask, MastodonMattermostPostNoticeTask, CountFileLinesTask, MattermostCustomerFeedbackAnalysisTask, MattermostBudgetApprovalPipelineTask, and MattermostCreateChannelTask**. All scored zero. Across all 19 internal retries, the saved backup trajectories are empty: the failures preceded model actions. No log establishes a scored MAI-UI task continuing after a mid-policy device-health failure. Nevertheless, result existence does not prove an unaffected environment. The additional descriptive sensitivity excluding all 16 MAI-UI tasks with a folder-level setup/scoring failure or internal health retry gives **11 vs v4 6 vs GUI-Owl 21 of 89**; this is an exclusion based on MAI-UI events, not proof that the retained environments were equivalent.
